<section class="sec" id="faq" style="background:#fff">
<div class="wrap">
<span class="eyebrow reveal">FAQ</span>
<h2 class="st reveal">The questions people actually <span class="serif">ask.</span></h2>
<p class="lede reveal">If yours isn't here, a counsellor answers it on a 20-minute call.</p>
<div class="faq-wrap">
<div class="acc reveal">
<details open=""><summary>Do I need coding or a math background to learn data analytics? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">No. The course starts from Excel and builds up. SQL is closer to structured English than programming, Power BI is visual, and Python arrives only in month three with full support. Comfort with numbers matters more than any degree.</div></details>
<details><summary>What will I actually learn in this course? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Advanced Excel, SQL end to end, Power BI with DAX, Python with pandas, practical statistics, AI-assisted analysis and data storytelling, finished with a presented capstone on a real business dataset.</div></details>
<details><summary>Which certification does this course prepare me for? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">The Microsoft PL-300 (Power BI Data Analyst Associate), the certification Indian recruiters ask for most. We build the prep into the course; the exam itself is booked with Microsoft and charged separately.</div></details>
<details><summary>What is the starting salary for a data analyst in India? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Freshers typically start between Rs 3.5 and 6 lakh depending on city and company. With two to three years and strong SQL, Rs 6 to 10 lakh is common, and senior analysts and BI developers earn well beyond that.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is data analytics still a good career now that AI can analyse data? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Yes, and arguably better. AI speeds up queries and charts, but companies need people who frame the question, verify the output and present the decision. We teach AI-assisted workflows from week one so you are the analyst who uses AI, not the one replaced by it.</div></details>
<details><summary>How long is the course and how much time do I need weekly? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Four months, around 204 hours across 10 modules and three capstones. Plan for roughly 8 hours a week of live sessions plus practice, scheduled so working professionals can keep up.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is it online or classroom, and is Malayalam support available? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Both. In-person batches run in Trivandrum, Kochi and Bengaluru, and live online batches across Kerala and the GCC. Sessions are in clear English with Malayalam support.</div></details>
